## Per-Table Lock Manager

This prevents the same table from being submitted multiple times before the previous run finishes.

```java
package com.example.datareader.reader;

import com.example.datareader.config.TableReaderProperties;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

import java.util.Set;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;

@Component
public class LocalTableLockManager {

    private final Set<String> runningJobs = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();

    public boolean tryLock(TableReaderProperties table) {
        return runningJobs.add(table.getJobKey());
    }

    public void unlock(TableReaderProperties table) {
        runningJobs.remove(table.getJobKey());
    }
}
```

This is safe for one application instance.

If you run multiple app instances, use a distributed lock such as:

* ShedLock
* Oracle lock table using `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`
* Redis lock
* PostgreSQL advisory lock if your metadata DB is PostgreSQL

